	abstract = {Drought is a major cause of yield reduction in a wide range of crops. Under the fast-changing climate scenario, drought episodes are expected to be more frequent, further penalizing crop yields. There is a need to enhance crop adaptation to drought for sustained productivity. Attempts have been made to validate and manipulate drought-traits in crops with some degree of success. There are evidence to show that plant and its associated microbiome interact and modulate traits in host plants. From this context, efforts are being made to manipulate drought traits using endophytes. In this review, we highlight the importance of associating endophytes with drought traits and the relevance of endophyte mediated manipulation of traits for crop production under water limiting conditions.},
