	url = {https://link.springer.com/10.1007/s12298-021-01123-x},
	doi = {10.1007/s12298-021-01123-x},
	abstract = {Abstract
            
              Plant cytoskeleton regulation has been studied using a new approach based on both (1) pharmacological analysis of tubulin and actin inhibitors and (2) mechanical stimulation achieved by using a slow-rotating (2 rpm) clinostat in combination with transcriptional analysis of genes encoding {TUA}6, {ACT}2, {MAP}65-1, {CLASP}, {PLDδ}, {FH}4 and {FH}1 proteins in
