              and
              {FH}1
              gene expression was noted during slow clinorotation, possibly due to altered mechanical impact on the cortical cytoskeleton. For the first time, the expression of the tubulin-associated gene
              {MAP}65-1
              was shown to be dependent upon the organization of {AFs}. {TUA}6, {MAP}65-1, {CLASP}, {FH}1 and {FH}4 likely participate in mechanical signal transduction. Our work demonstrated that slow clinorotation is able to cause mechanical stress.},
